  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="a22f-ad2a-c85a-d2ff" name="Early Imperial Roman (AoA2) - List Notes" publicationId="fcb9-17be-94c2-bcfc" hidden="false">
      <description>ARMIES OF ANTIQUITY v2 #45 (unofficial, Martin Gibbins). This list takes the army from the triumph of Augustus to the time of Septimius Severus. The backbone of the army in this period is the legionary infantry, but its supports have become more regular and the cavalry is much improved. Apart from the civil war of 69AD the Roman state was largely stable during this period. Imperial expansion continued for over a hundred years, the last conquest being that of Dacia by Trajan. Numerii: Warriors 5 3 3 3 3 1 3 1 5 7 Numerii: Light Infantry 5 3 3 3 3 1 3 1 5 9 Numerii: Skirmishers 5 3 3 3 3 1 3 1 5 8 Numerii: Warriors have hand weapon, throwing spear, shield, Warband, and may have light armour (+2). Numerii: Light Infantry have hand weapons, javelins, shield, Light Infantry, Warband, and may have throwing spear (+3). Numerii: Skirmishers have hand weapons, javelins, buckler, Skirmish, Warband, and may exchange javelins for sling (-1) or bow (free) and lose Warband.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Early Imperial Roman - Early Army 30 BC to 110 AD]
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Characters: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 20% Cavalry: Up to 25% Infantry: At least 50% Artillery: Up to one machine per 800 points Allies: Up to 25%: Armenian or Maccabean lists
[Early Imperial Roman - Later Army 110 AD to 193 AD]
  Cavalry: up to 50%
  Characters: up to 20%
  Characters: up to 20% Cavalry: Up to 50% Infantry: At least 33% Artillery: Up to one machine per 800 points Allies: None</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
